{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential","id":590340,"title":"Wasted Potential","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-14T11:31:59-07:00","id":590340,"title":"Wasted Potential","content":"This is something that struck me when I read The King's Raven's topic on the Counterculture USA Micro Dark Era project. Specifically, their notes about their planned Spirit Scapers compact being their personal replacement for the Keepers of the Source.<br /> <br /> Now, I'll be honest: I've always hated the Keepers. They just do NOT make any sense to me. Hippy hunters is one thing, but a hunter compact based on a number of people having a very specific form of Unseen Senses? I could buy a Cell with their background, but not a Compact.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the Spirit Scapers DO make sense to me. They still have some fundamental flaws with their ideology - &quot;positive&quot; spirits being no less monstrous than negative ones means that, really, they're not going to undercut the fundamental problems of human/spirit interactions - but, at the same time, their ideology makes sense and is believable (which is more than can be said of the Keepers). It genuinely is possible to affect each world by manipulating the other, and so negative spirits like hate, rape, murder, pollution, lies, etc can be driven off and positive ones of love, peace, joy, family, etc can be attracted, and even if positive spirits are still inclined to Urge, Ride and Claim, well, they do generally make the world better through their presence, so it's not an inherently stupid idea to want to manipulate the spiritual environment to encourage their presence and dissuade the negative spirits. Their clash with werewolves and mages genuinely becomes gray, as the Spirit Scapers really are doing much the same things as these monsters are, in stark contrast to the Keepers.<br /> <br /> Now, anyway, the point behind this topic is this: what compacts, conspiracies, plot hooks or other general ideas do you think Hunter has that it really could have done better? The King's Raven and I have both observed the wasted potential of the &quot;Hippy Hunters&quot; as evidenced through the Keeprs of the Source, and TKR is fixing that in their homebrew with the Spirit Scapers, but what have you other Hunter STs fixed on as &quot;could have been done better&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T11:39:46-07:00","id":590363,"title":"","content":"The Ascending Ones. They're three poorly-defined groups stapled together; are they nodern alchemists, are they drug dealers and gang members, or are they Islamic hunters? All if them at once, with no organization or central authority. Bleuch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T13:18:44-07:00","id":590445,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the kind words VoidDrifter.<br /> <br /> Division Six: They don't have much VALKARIE don't, except that they're pawns of a Seer (which is something that belongs in Mage books not Hunter) and the technocracy shout outs. Looking at the picture it's clear that the book is sneering at them; which is always a bad idea. I can't see any way of redeeming them.<br /> <br /> Knights of Saint George: The problem I see is that these guys don't really fit into or say anything about the themes of Mage. They're just a group who hunt and kill mages. I'd much rather focus directly on the idea of Truth; with a Hunter Conspiracy that is making a coherent argument that Lies can be better than Truth.<br /> <br /> Aegis Kai Doru: I feel like there's a lot of focus on the least interesting parts of this group - collecting Relics, and their hatred of Werewolves and Mages. I'd rather focus on the fact that they see the long term view (they're both ancient and archeologists). And their internal philosophy which really needs to be more than just hating Werewolves and Mages. My solution would be to give them a belief that they could rebuild whatever ancient utopia they believe they came from with the right relics; and drop the grudge with monsters only being important if the monsters get between the AKD and their Relics.<br /> <br /> Les Mysteres: The unification of just about shamanism concept ever is basically nonsensical. I dislike the whole manipulated by spirits angle too; hunters being manipulated by monsters (in protagonist sections of Hunter books) is a deal breaker for me. I'd fix that by making them purely Voodoo; I'd keep the spirit manipulation but make it more of a risk to individuals rather than a something that's happened to the group. I'd make their conflict about them breaching the gauntlet. (Oh, a big sidebar about Loa; there's a good one in Second Sight that can be copied - but maybe mention the Empyerian and Inferno in that sidebar)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=590363#post590363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ascending Ones. They're three poorly-defined groups stapled together; are they nodern alchemists, are they drug dealers and gang members, or are they Islamic hunters? All if them at once, with no organization or central authority. Bleuch.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're an alliance of multiple groups. A few drug cartells, a few orders of (mostly Islamic) assassin/Hunters, a few ancient societies of alchemists. It could be made clearer but they're one of my favourites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T14:19:50-07:00","id":590484,"title":"","content":"We have done this a million times already. The number 1 topic on this forum seems to be people whining about this or that group not matching their personal preferences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T14:23:48-07:00","id":590488,"title":"","content":"That's because sharing our preferences is always fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T14:45:21-07:00","id":590504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=590363#post590363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ascending Ones. They're three poorly-defined groups stapled together; are they modern alchemists, are they drug dealers and gang members, or are they Islamic hunters? All if them at once, with no organization or central authority. Bleuch.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are one ancient tradition that took on multiple forms out of their ancient roots and might be on the verge of breaking apart in a multitude of compacts/factions, depending on how one looks at it. Drugs could be seen as the province of alchemy or mystery cults in all too many periods of human history, not to mention the separation between a gang, warrior society or hunter cell can be paper-thin depending on context. The Ascending Ones touch upon these things and also how compacts may change while still pursuing the Vigil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T15:03:45-07:00","id":590522,"title":"","content":"Major hopes from 2e: making VALKYRIE feel more like a government task force and less like &quot;your cell, but with fancy guns,&quot; giving the AKD a greater feeling of history (and ties to Mummy, not Werewolf of all things), and making Les Mysteres explicitly tied to vodoun and the loa, not &quot;all of the shamans ever.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T16:49:43-07:00","id":590586,"title":"","content":"<b>Aegis Kai Doru</b><br /> <br /> I like much of the AKD background and flavor, but their choice of supernatural opponents felt kind of awkward and forced. I my games I re-focused them more squarely on Relics.<br /> Between the major splats and general WoD weirdness, the world would be crawling with supernatural items. Some are innocuous, many are dangerous, and a few are apocalyptic. I moved the AKD in a sort of &quot;Warehouse 13/ Friday the 13th: the Series&quot; niche where their days are spent tracking down these things to keep them out of the wrong hands.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T18:07:26-07:00","id":590658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=590445#post590445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the kind words VoidDrifter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe in giving credit where it's due. I'm looking forward to seeing the Spirit Scapers because, yeah, Keepers are pretty much my go to for &quot;stupidest, most hamhanded creation of Hunter&quot; and I'd love to see Hippy Hunters I can actually buy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=590445#post590445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Division Six: They don't have much VALKARIE don't, except that they're pawns of a Seer (which is something that belongs in Mage books not Hunter) and the technocracy shout outs. Looking at the picture it's clear that the book is sneering at them; which is always a bad idea. I can't see any way of redeeming them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm not exactly a huge MtAs fan, but as far as I can see, Division Six is just a really, really lame Take That flavored cancer cell compact. If they were a legitimate military force, say researchers trying to understand what magic is or which is dedicated to hunting down Abyssal paradoxes and the spirit possessed, maybe they could be saved. Emphasis on the maybe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=590445#post590445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Knights of Saint George: The problem I see is that these guys don't really fit into or say anything about the themes of Mage. They're just a group who hunt and kill mages. I'd much rather focus directly on the idea of Truth; with a Hunter Conspiracy that is making a coherent argument that Lies can be better than Truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah... I mean, maybe they'd be a little better if they were more obviously tied to the Abyss, but even then they'd be pretty sour. Tying them to the Lie, or even merging them with Division Six's on-paper goal (the belief that &quot;this reality is just fine, we don't need you making things worse by fiddling with it!&quot;) would probably be a better use for them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=590445#post590445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aegis Kai Doru: I feel like there's a lot of focus on the least interesting parts of this group - collecting Relics, and their hatred of Werewolves and Mages. I'd rather focus on the fact that they see the long term view (they're both ancient and archeologists). And their internal philosophy which really needs to be more than just hating Werewolves and Mages. My solution would be to give them a belief that they could rebuild whatever ancient utopia they believe they came from with the right relics; and drop the grudge with monsters only being important if the monsters get between the AKD and their Relics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely agree with the whole &quot;relic gatherers, not disgruntled haters for werewolves and mages&quot;. Hell, by the rules as written, they can't even TOUCH actual Awakened relics without destroying them due to that pesky Paradox. They should be much more focused on mummy-fighting, and even then that's only because mummies are the major splat for producing &amp; interacting with relics; they still opportunistically go after every magical item they can. Seriously, unless the 2e update changes things, mages should probably be their least-involved splat, since their relics would (ironically) get a reputation as less reliable than changeling tokens or werewolf fetishes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=590445#post590445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Les Mysteres: The unification of just about shamanism concept ever is basically nonsensical. I dislike the whole manipulated by spirits angle too; hunters being manipulated by monsters (in protagonist sections of Hunter books) is a deal breaker for me. I'd fix that by making them purely Voodoo; I'd keep the spirit manipulation but make it more of a risk to individuals rather than a something that's happened to the group. I'd make their conflict about them breaching the gauntlet. (Oh, a big sidebar about Loa; there's a good one in Second Sight that can be copied - but maybe mention the Empyerian and Inferno in that sidebar)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... honestly, I'm of two minds when it comes to Les Mysteres.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, I agree they make no sense as a Compact. The basic idea, that religious individuals who practice in the right ways open themselves up to the very real spirits of the WoD, is certainly sound, but... we can't get two individuals from two faiths to agree in the real world. In the WoD, where A: people are bigger assholes in general, and B: these religious nuts have &quot;proof&quot; that their faith is the &quot;one true faith&quot;, I certainly would consider it more likely that they'd tear each other apart than work together.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the basic existence of Les Mysteres make a lot of sense to me. I don't mind the being manipulated by spirits thing because, honestly, that's what's going to happen. It IS possible to bind spirits, IF you have the right occultic knowledge to do so and manage to get very lucky. But when you're coming at things from the angle of &quot;the spirits are good and holy and must be obeyed and respected&quot;, if you believe because of your faith that the spirits are inherently better than you, then you are giving the spirits an edge in your dealings with them. Even if your rituals do manage to bind them, if you let your beliefs bind you to the lies they spill and to the reality of their ecosystem, well, the ball's in their court. For the same reason, if you believe because of your faith that the spirits are good and/or a necessary part of the world's health, then of course you're going to mix up the Pure and the Forsaken - one side is revering the spirits like you do, the other is setting themselves up as superior to the spirits. You view the world through the lens of faith rather than fact, you're going to make decisions that are factually wrong.<br /> <br /> It's annoying to play the dupe, but let's be honest; the compacts &amp; conspiracies are written up as much for NPC potential as for player potential. Les Mysteres are a PERFECT example of a hostile Hunter organization to use in a Werewolf game, or a cancer cell in a Hunter game. I'd never want to play a member of Les Mysteres, but then, I'd never want to play a member of the Malleus Maleficarium or the Long Night either, as religious-based hunters in general tend to make my guts roil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T18:13:28-07:00","id":590663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=590363#post590363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ascending Ones. They're three poorly-defined groups stapled together; are they nodern alchemists, are they drug dealers and gang members, or are they Islamic hunters? All if them at once, with no organization or central authority. Bleuch.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the fractional nature of The Ascending Ones is a sad consequence of what they are. I mean, if you go; &quot;They're Alchemists!&quot; then that begs the question &quot;Ok, how're they tied to Prometheans, the mainline who runs with the whole Alchemist thing?&quot;. If you go &quot;They're Islamic Hunters!&quot; then that begs the question &quot;How do we portray this in a way that doesn't get Onyx Paths HQ blown up by extreamists?&quot;. If you go &quot;They're drug dealers and gangsters!&quot; then that begs the question; &quot;How are they a Conspiracy, and not a Compact then?&quot;<br /> <br /> Personally, I really like The Ascending Ones, but I think you need to choose one of those 3 options and focus almost exclusively on that in your own game to really make them work. Probably one of the first two are the way to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T20:46:20-07:00","id":590784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=590363#post590363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ascending Ones. They're three poorly-defined groups stapled together; are they nodern alchemists, are they drug dealers and gang members, or are they Islamic hunters? All if them at once, with no organization or central authority. Bleuch.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the C&amp;C book actually nailed this one by making the juxtaposition of their 3 factions centrally thematic to them.<br /> <br /> But basically they click once you realize they're the MYTHIC Hashashins (Ahl al-Jabal are based on the historically accurate medieval Nizari Ismailis) - so ancient cult of alchemists and religious mystics goes together, and the drug cartels/street gangs are how they weave themselves through the modern world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T23:27:09-07:00","id":590962,"title":"","content":"I put in a pitch to get hired for Hunter if it's happening this year. I have hopes of working on the AKD and Ascending ones with an eye of bringing out the awesomeness of both these groups.<br /> <br /> This, of course, depends on me getting hired.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T00:22:10-07:00","id":591004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=590658#post590658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm looking forward to seeing the Spirit Scapers because</div> </div> </div> </div> Don't hold your breath; I don't have any plans to expand upon what I've already written at the moment.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=590658#post590658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;the spirits are good and holy and must be obeyed and respected&quot;,</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why voodoo is a good choice; it acknowledges that the Loa can be flawed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=590663#post590663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I really like The Ascending Ones, but I think you need to choose one of those 3 options and focus almost exclusively on that in your own game to really make them work. Probably one of the first two are the way to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and know. If you're playing the Ascending Ones you should pick one of the three; but that's because they're an allience of many different groups so don't remove the others; just make it clear which group your players come from.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T05:27:12-07:00","id":591160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=590363#post590363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ascending Ones. They're three poorly-defined groups stapled together; are they nodern alchemists, are they drug dealers and gang members, or are they Islamic hunters? All if them at once, with no organization or central authority. Bleuch.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm with King's Raven on this. They <i>are</i> three groups, and their history has led them to mostly merge. (If it was me, I might reflect this by having the middle Status benefit* vary by which one you're part of). And I think that's a good thing, because real world secret societies do fission and fuse, and change.<br /> <br /> * And the first one; if compacts can get their own Endowments these days, then conspiracies ought to get a Status 1 benefit independent of theirs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=590445#post590445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Division Six: They don't have much VALKARIE don't, except that they're pawns of a Seer (which is something that belongs in Mage books not Hunter) and the technocracy shout outs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Strictly speaking, they <i>were</i> pawns of a Seer, but have grown well out of his control. Also, I disagree that no groups ever should be compromised (though my personal approach would be each group getting a &quot;which type of monster is most likely to have taken it over and why&quot; sidebar). Other than those quibbles, I don't like them either.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Knights of Saint George: The problem I see is that these guys don't really fit into or say anything about the themes of Mage. They're just a group who hunt and kill mages. I'd much rather focus directly on the idea of Truth; with a Hunter Conspiracy that is making a coherent argument that Lies can be better than Truth. </div> </div> </div>They do see a &quot;true reality,&quot; only it's a true reality made of horrible shit that mages are attracting to the Earth. (In Mage terms, they're functionally replacing the Supernal with the Abyss as the truth, and finding Earth a better lie than the ones the mages tell). Works for me.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Aegis Kai Doru... My solution would be to give them a belief that they could rebuild whatever ancient utopia they believe they came from with the right relics; and drop the grudge with monsters only being important if the monsters get between the AKD and their Relics. </div> </div> </div>I rather like that. It's also a nice way to tie them to Mummy.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Les Mysteres: The unification of just about shamanism concept ever is basically nonsensical. I dislike the whole manipulated by spirits angle too; hunters being manipulated by monsters (in protagonist sections of Hunter books) is a deal breaker for me. </div> </div> </div>Again, I don't hold that no group should be compromised ever. And Spirit Slayers, by virtue of getting werewolves and spirits into one supplement - which are, from a hunting the supernatural perspective, pretty much opposites - has to be a bit more beholden to Werewolf than Night Stalkers and Witch Finders do to Vampire and Mage, which means the spirits being bad news.<br /> However, werewolf itself provides one possible solution to this, in that spirits have a major case of you are what you eat. When Blasphemies talks about spirit cults, it includes a note that if a spirit primarily gets its essence from a group of worshippers, then even if it started out conning them, it won't be long before it's a believer as well.<br /> <br /> The pan-shamanism has to go, I agree there. Afro-Caribbean would be my choice as well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T10:34:46-07:00","id":591439,"title":"","content":"I actually really like the Knights of St. George. Witnessing magic is damaging to the souls of the uninitiated, and it's easy to imagine the Knights as a group of individuals so deeply scarred by their interactions with the Supernal that they've turned away from it entirely, toward the Abyss or some kind of twisted Lower Depth. In a way, they fit the themes of Mage by acting as the antithesis of the Awakened; Mages boldly strive for higher truths, while the Knights are driven by fear and ignorance to destroy truth-seekers in the hopes of appeasing faceless gods that they can't begin to comprehend. They can also represent an object lesson in the consequences of hubris, both by embodying the horrifying consequences of exposing Sleepers to magic and by actively punishing Mages who practice their art too openly.<br /> <br /> At the same time, I find the Knights sympathetic, in a sad sort of way. They're underdogs struggling (at least in their own view) to save the world from forces far beyond what they can comprehend or directly oppose. They're trying to be heroes, but they're too damaged to realize that they they became villains a long time ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T11:19:52-07:00","id":591564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=591160#post591160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strictly speaking, they <i>were</i> pawns of a Seer, but have grown well out of his control.</div> </div> </div> </div> Were they? I think that he's riding a tiger but he's still in control and picking the targets.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=591160#post591160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I disagree that no groups ever should be compromised (though my personal approach would be each group getting a &quot;which type of monster is most likely to have taken it over and why&quot; sidebar).</div> </div> </div> </div> I never said that Hunters can't be compromised; simply that compromised groups belong in antagonist chapters rather than protragonist chapters.<br /> <br /> My preferred solution would be to have an evil mirror universe equivilant to each group. I just think giving them different names would be useful so people can refer to one or the other easily, also it lets you get in a paragraph or two about what the monster wants. The Guardians of the Pyramid are still questing for a special set of Relics; but they don't want to rebuilt utopia. They want to destroy the world. No world, no Sekhem, and then their Mummy lord gets his revenge against the Judges.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=591160#post591160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">has to be a bit more beholden to Werewolf than Night Stalkers and Witch Finders do to Vampire and Mage, which means the spirits being bad news.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not nesecarally. Spirits are dangerous, but not evil. There is more than one way of managing them.<br /> <br /> It takes a lot of wisdom and strength to allow spirits to ride, to guide humanity, without Spirits going too far. But it also takes a lot of strength and wisdom to protect the Gauntlet. If Les Mysteries are good enough they could do it.<br /> <br /> And anyway. Maybe the Loa are different from Spirits and the Werewolves are the ones who're wrong to say Loa are bad news like spirits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=591439#post591439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a way, they fit the themes of Mage by acting as the antithesis of the Awakened; Mages boldly strive for higher truths, while the Knights are driven by fear and ignorance to destroy truth-seekers in the hopes of appeasing faceless gods that they can't begin to comprehend.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's more fitting the setting than fitting the themes IMO. They don't really say anything that the Mage books aren't already saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-15-2015, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T11:39:23-07:00","id":591591,"title":"","content":"Personally, I like most of the hunter groups- including the Witch Finder ones. One group I do see as &quot;wasted potential&quot; is the Heritage House from Glimpses of the Unknown- I mean, 90% of the people don't even remember them! Their &quot;theme&quot; is too weak, and the fluff around them is already covered by a number of other groups. If you get a wordcount for a new hunter group, please use it wisely :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T14:37:53-07:00","id":591796,"title":"","content":"Has anyone tinkered with the Aves Minerva around here? And with a name like that, could they have some sort of connection to the Strix, or in a contrary tack, some of the &quot;original strix&quot; have been servants of her in the past?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T15:11:45-07:00","id":591921,"title":"","content":"I disagree about a group being compromised meaning it shouldn't be in the protagonist section. generally, I dont play with characters in a compromised group knowing the group is compromised, and generally groups are not avid about knowing their compromise, but having the storyteller know and having it be &quot;canon&quot; for a lack of a better term can lead to fun and interesting stories. the idea that TFV was created by vampires to enforce the masquerade is pretty awesome to me, Hunters in groups are almost certainly going to be co-opted by the more subtle supernatural monsters, the monsters just cant help themselves, its too easy to direct this vicious weapon against their enemies","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5718-hackthulhu","name":"Hackthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T17:01:01-07:00","id":592066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=591564#post591564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's more fitting the setting than fitting the themes IMO. They don't really say anything that the Mage books aren't already saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, firstly, the Knights are from Hunter, and I feel like they fit many of the Hunter themes, like fighting against long odds and struggling (with mixed success) to fight monsters without becoming a monster yourself, quite well.<br /> <br /> That said, I do think they have something interesting to offer a Mage game as well. Most of the antagonists mages regularly face are either other mages or arise directly from the use of Awakened magic. Sleepers, on the other hand, often come off as either an annoyance (because they screw up your magic), or as poor unfortunate souls in need of guidance and protection so their fragile little brains don't break under the pressure of Supernal truth.<br /> <br /> The Knights, however, demonstrate that Sleepers can be more than just passive bystanders, and that hubris has consequences more far-reaching than Mages usually realize. Expose too many sleepers to Awakened magic, and they might just come back and slit your throat on the pieces of their broken souls.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=591796#post591796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone tinkered with the Aves Minerva around here? And with a name like that, could they have some sort of connection to the Strix, or in a contrary tack, some of the &quot;original strix&quot; have been servants of her in the past?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh... I'm not too keen on the Strix being anybody's servants (collectively, I mean; there are certainly ways to enslave specific members of the species), or on the idea of every single owl-related thing being connected to the Strix. That said, I could see Vampires (at least those in the know about the Strix) becoming really paranoid when their Kindred start disappearing and owl symbols start showing up more and more in the local graffiti, or what have you. The Aves, in turn, might realize that (some) Vampires have a weird phobia of owls, even if they don't know the specific reason, and might try to use that to their advantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 07-15-2015, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T19:07:21-07:00","id":592209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=592066#post592066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh... I'm not too keen on the Strix being anybody's servants (collectively, I mean; there are certainly ways to enslave specific members of the species), or on the idea of every single owl-related thing being connected to the Strix. That said, I could see Vampires (at least those in the know about the Strix) becoming really paranoid when their Kindred start disappearing and owl symbols start showing up more and more in the local graffiti, or what have you. The Aves, in turn, might realize that (some) Vampires have a weird phobia of owls, even if they don't know the specific reason, and might try to use that to their advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet curiously, some strix themselves seems to make implications about lost homes, duties &amp; masters in Wicked Dead. But then, who says all strix are honest or all the same. It's perfectly possible the strix tormenting the kindred at present are <b>not</b> the same as the Julii nemeses, as a whole at least - the differences in both appearance (<b>crows</b>, <b>ravens</b>, <b>vultures </b>&amp; owls) and capacity between Requiem to Rome and Wicked Dead could very well reflect the possibility they are different but similar beings the kindred have conflated with the old strix folklore of yore.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Aves were a compact during roman republic &amp; empire times striking at kindred and other supernaturals, what actually makes the connection feasible, even if it was just a lone strix messing with mortals with fake prophecies and divine guidance to make some special pawns.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T00:44:29-07:00","id":592395,"title":"","content":"I won't deny that it's plausible that there's some connection; I guess I personally prefer to separate the owl as a symbol of wisdom from the &quot;bird of ill omen&quot; archetype. That said, since the Strix were directly inspired by classical mythology, I think it would be a mistake to present the nemeses of Roman times from their later incarnations. Rather, I get the sense that the idea of the Strix has evolved with each book they've appeared in, and I prefer the current presentation of them as something timeless and intrinsically tied to the Kindred over the idea that they're some kind of supernatural servants or weapons that somehow slipped the leash.<br /> <br /> In any event, the beautiful thing about the nWoD is that you can make whatever you want out of the pieces presented in the books, and the Aves are mysterious enough that they could be made into almost anything. It might be worth noting, however, that as far as I can recall they're described (in Night Stalkers, I think?) as having access to some kind of ritual magic, which would technically make them a conspiracy rather than a compact. I think there was some suggestion that the Cainite Heresy later co-opted some of their magical secrets, but I could be mistaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T01:40:56-07:00","id":592408,"title":"","content":"From one side, one needs to be blind to ignore the similarity between the Aves Minerva and the Strixs- the original presentation of the strixs was beings of Roman origin (during that time they were called striges, after all- the Latin name for Owls. Yeah, later incarnations say that they can show up as other birds, but the very meaning of their name is Owl) who are antagonistic toward vampires and are connected to weird blood magics. The Aves Minerva means the Birds of Minerva, which are owls, and they are antagonistic toward vampires and use some weird blood sorcery. Heck, the original writeup of them even has a VII Endowment!..<br /> <br /> But that writeup also denies any kind of connection between the Owls and the Birds. The Aves even clain to hate the Owls for taking the form of their goddess. Plus, why the hell would the strixs give so much help for those crazy humans without taking their skin and dance with it? Shouldn't they be bored already? And how they track down every member of the Heresy and give them their weird Blood Magics? And what they drink tea with the crazy demon and pervert ghoul in Italy?...<br /> <br /> In sort, there is no canon connection between the Cainte Heresy and the Aves Minerva to the strixs any more then there is a canon connection between the Knights of St George and the Abyss- but it can be implied or read this way. You can take it or leave it, but I like patterns and the pattern is this: each hunter specialized group use their enemy's enemy for help. The Knights call upon the Abyss. Les Mysteres use Spirits. Faithful of Shulpae belong to the Devourer. Knights of St Adrian work with the Machine. And the Cainte? They come from the strixs. Again, this is not written explicitly, and heck maybe that pattern is just like seeing faces on the Moon- but you can use it. Nothing in the text approve or deny it, so you can take it or leave it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T05:30:37-07:00","id":592539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential#post590340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is something that struck me when I read The King's Raven's topic on the Counterculture USA Micro Dark Era project. Specifically, their notes about their planned Spirit Scapers compact being their personal replacement for the Keepers of the Source.<br /> <br /> Now, I'll be honest: I've always hated the Keepers. They just do NOT make any sense to me. Hippy hunters is one thing, but a hunter compact based on a number of people having a very specific form of Unseen Senses? I could buy a Cell with their background, but not a Compact.</div> </div> </div> </div> You do get that so many of them have that form of unseen senses because they were taught it, right? <br /> <br /> And Cell level is &quot;guy with a baseball bat,&quot; not &quot;guy who was taught a minor supernatural merit.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T09:41:37-07:00","id":592786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=592066#post592066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, firstly, the Knights are from Hunter, and I feel like they fit many of the Hunter themes, like fighting against long odds and struggling (with mixed success) to fight monsters without becoming a monster yourself, quite well.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's actually not how the Hunter groups are supposed to work. We're up to around 30 groups now; there's only so many different ways you can spin long odds, fighting monsters, and fearing becoming a monster. That's why diversity is the name of the Hunter game. Even in the corebook you have groups who're not primarally about fighting monsters (Null Mysteries, Network Zero, the Ascending Ones on occasion).<br /> <br /> The splat-focused suppliments are supposed to express that by tying into the themes of the game they fight. Take Night Stalkers:<ul><li>The Barret Commission play the same power games as vampires.</li> <li>If vampires are parasitical elites feeding off the downtrodden then Night Watch are those down trodden striking back.</li> <li>The Canite Herasy are explicitly victims to parallel the Vampires-as-an-victimiser metaphor. They also live lives of isolation and mobility, the opposite of a vampire in an entrenched power structure.</li> <li>The Maidens Blood Sisterhood are feminists to contrast to the Vampires-as-rapists metaphor.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> But Witch Finders doesn't really offer me that kind of interesting thematic ties. Promethian Brotherhood excepted; they're just hunters who kill witches, nothing more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=592066#post592066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Knights, however, demonstrate that Sleepers can be more than just passive bystanders, and that hubris has consequences more far-reaching than Mages usually realize. Expose too many sleepers to Awakened magic, and they might just come back and slit your throat on the pieces of their broken souls.</div> </div> </div> </div> Isn't that Banishers?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T15:06:19-07:00","id":593200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=592786#post592786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't that Banishers?</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that banishers come from failed or refused awakenings... I very well might be wrong, but the KoSG would be different if they are people who are molded and seen by Paradox... also they are all a single bloodline going back to king arthur (or so they claim) so more like the banisher version of Proximi maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5718-hackthulhu","name":"Hackthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T19:13:20-07:00","id":593462,"title":"","content":"Yes, Banishers are from broken awakenings, and exist to destroy magic. They are essentially crazy mages.<br /> <br /> Knights of St George have that neat balance that hunter does well, in that they're wrong but not completely wrong. There's a lot of stuff in the World of Darkness and a lot of things are depicted as having the entire picture, even when it doesn't really fit. When hunters are depicted as having a part of the picture and working with what they've got, it makes sense. Especially when that point of view can't be dismissed by readily-accessible proof. The Knights are wrong in thinking that Mages are actively bringing destruction into the world, but they're not completely wrong because that's what paradox and the Scelesti do. In addition they have found a way to take advantage of power from within themselves. Good on them.<br /> <br /> Back on topic, I think the Loyalists of Thule are a bit out of touch. It always seemed to me like it was put in to have an excuse to have some sort of Nazi-related group and I have a hard time seeing how it would last more than two generations and exist in modern nights.<br /> <br /> Also the Cainite Heresy. They have some nice background that hooks them into other settings. They have interesting abilities and a focus and reason, ample fodder for recruits among those harmed by vampires. But they're a suicide cult, and they seem so aggressive that they don't really fit very well unless you're playing a very specific kind of game. They seem more fitting for a vampire antagonist than as a vampire hunter group. Especially since their brand of zealotry is something you could slap onto an individual character from almost any other conspiracy and compact and not have it be that out of the ordinary before having a whole legion of secret suicide killers.<br /> <br /> On the opposite side of things, Network Zero always seemed to go a little too far. Taking a video of something and putting it up on youtube is easy. Everyone who sees it may not be shocked into sudden belief in all things supernatural, but at least someone out there will believe it. In Vampire the Requiem you don't have the world-spanning Camarilla there pulling strings alongside the Technocracy to get things shut down, so it seems like their job would be relatively easy, especially if they just kept on the road. This puts a huge burden on the storyteller. 'Why isn't my video of a coterie of vampires fighting the trio of wizards we lured them into getting anyone to believe in vampires or wizards?' The idea of full-on revelation is a potentially world-shattering concept, and that's a bit much for a compact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T23:49:53-07:00","id":593608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=593462#post593462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the opposite side of things, Network Zero always seemed to go a little too far. Taking a video of something and putting it up on youtube is easy. Everyone who sees it may not be shocked into sudden belief in all things supernatural, but at least someone out there will believe it. In Vampire the Requiem you don't have the world-spanning Camarilla there pulling strings alongside the Technocracy to get things shut down, so it seems like their job would be relatively easy, especially if they just kept on the road. This puts a huge burden on the storyteller. 'Why isn't my video of a coterie of vampires fighting the trio of wizards we lured them into getting anyone to believe in vampires or wizards?' The idea of full-on revelation is a potentially world-shattering concept, and that's a bit much for a compact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you don't <i>need</i> a world spanning Camarilla or Technocracy (though there are the Seer Ministries), single Vampire with the right connections of a Mage with Forces could remove it. But, really, why would they bother? <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=proof+vampires+exist\" target=\"_blank\">There are 5,020 results for the Youtube search &quot;proof vampires exist&quot;</a>, how many of those do you believe? As you said, <i>anyone</i> can post a Youtube video, including crazy people that the vast majority of people don't take seriously.<br /> <br /> But Network Zero knows it's in for the long haul, the slow conversion. They don't sit their wondering why millions of people aren't shocked into suddenly knowing the truth, they're hoping that just one person sees their video and starts to believe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T09:02:38-07:00","id":593868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=593608#post593608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, you don't <i>need</i> a world spanning Camarilla or Technocracy (though there are the Seer Ministries), single Vampire with the right connections of a Mage with Forces could remove it. But, really, why would they bother? <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=proof+vampires+exist\" target=\"_blank\">There are 5,020 results for the Youtube search &quot;proof vampires exist&quot;</a>, how many of those do you believe? As you said, <i>anyone</i> can post a Youtube video, including crazy people that the vast majority of people don't take seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you seen them, though? They're not even remotely proof. It's people talking to the camera and telling vampire stories or blurry video of animal attacks, one is a video of a bat stuck on the ground trying to get to the air, not even counting the hundreds, if not thousands, of results that have nothing to do with vampires that come up from that search, like 'Uma Thurman immortal or time traveler'. It would be much more believable if there was an actual vampire doing actual vampire things. Issues with the law are something supernaturals have to deal with now. Commit crimes, and you don't have a world power at your back capable of telling an entire police department or news agency to be quiet about it. But when it comes to proof from Network Zero, a ST has to make up alliances between vampires and mages. This is what I was saying, it puts a huge burden on the storyteller to constantly block the character's every effort to do what their compact is about doing. Why should anyone play that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-17-2015, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T09:53:13-07:00","id":593898,"title":"","content":"1) It's worth noting that while there may or may not be supernatural efforts towards keeping the secrecy, Valkyrie's goal is to conflict with the supernatural while maintaining their secrecy, with an entire branch devoted to covering shit up. Between that and groups tendency to prefer being quiet and usual human interests, you might not need much more.<br /> <br /> 2) It really is that last part that's hard to push. Even in a world where everyone sort of knows that there's something in the dark, most people just aren't willing to invest in it.<br /> <br /> THe big thing NetZo has to deal with indifference and 'disbelief', followed by the response time of groups like Valkyrie.<br /> <br /> 3)And for making it clear, NetZo has to attain three things to make their dreams come true: credibility, collaborative numerical mass(Or basically a large number of regular material that corresponds with one another and strengthens the argument), and popularity(essentially, because I can't remember a better word for widespread throughout the world). That's, by itself, problematic enough, and having TFV and other parties move against them doesn't help, BUT!<br /> <br /> 4)NetZo has one big advantage, and it's huge-they're riding the cutting edge wave of the communication boom. Every new way that the anarchic communication community is grabbed and used, and no force in the world can keep up with the sort of people NetZo has taking advantage of this. THey don't need to keep stuff up for long, just long enough to catch attention. Even with later discrediting, If people can see something long enough for people to ask questions about it, then they've made a significant push against the tide. They keep that up enough, and they will win the fight against the ocean. And with that said, that cutting edge is a hell of advantage. It really does by them more time than people think, and sets the foot in the door to keep kicking.<br /> <br /> NetZo could do well with aligning with groups like Null Mysteriis for credibility, but right now their fight is just fighting every thing that says &quot;THis must be secret&quot;, and the truth is they're kind of winning on that front.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T10:14:40-07:00","id":593910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=593868#post593868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you seen them, though? They're not even remotely proof. It's people talking to the camera and telling vampire stories or blurry video of animal attacks, one is a video of a bat stuck on the ground trying to get to the air, not even counting the hundreds, if not thousands, of results that have nothing to do with vampires that come up from that search, like 'Uma Thurman immortal or time traveler'. It would be much more believable if there was an actual vampire doing actual vampire things. Issues with the law are something supernaturals have to deal with now. Commit crimes, and you don't have a world power at your back capable of telling an entire police department or news agency to be quiet about it. But when it comes to proof from Network Zero, a ST has to make up alliances between vampires and mages. This is what I was saying, it puts a huge burden on the storyteller to constantly block the character's every effort to do what their compact is about doing. Why should anyone play that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires are impossible to capture properly on camera (unless they suppress it, iirc) and seeing obvious magic would trigger Quiescence and make you rationalize away what you just saw.<br /> <br /> Combine that with the existence of CGI and /shrug.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T10:28:21-07:00","id":593942,"title":"","content":"Due to the nature of the internet, you don't actually <i>need</i> a global conspiracy to combat a group like Network Zero. Focusing on Vampires for the moment, the writeup for the Mission in <i>Blood and Smoke </i>describes the local Invictus as having seemingly declared war on the internet. They most likely use a combination of automated scripts and human monitors to keep an eye on certain types of web videos, and have agents in the offices of Youtube and Google tasked with making sure that major potential Masquerade breaches get taken down for &quot;terms of service violations.&quot; If the videos wind up being hosted someplace that the Invictus can't shut them down, they can always resort to DDOS attacks or have their agents try to hack the server.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, you've got Project: ADAMSKI making sure that Youtube is <i>always</i> flooded with obviously fake &quot;proof vampires exist&quot; videos, so that Masquerade-breaking content is unlikely to gain much traction before somebody notices them and takes them down.<br /> <br /> That said, Youtube hasn't proven itself to be entirely successful in combating copyright violations, and they'd probably have the same problem with Masquerade breaches if enough people were dedicated to keeping them up (which, thanks to NetZo, they are). Furthermore, there are probably NetZo cells specifically dedicated to exposing Vampiric corruption within the internet services that they rely on, making the Invictus' job harder. NetZo probably has its own hackers as well, working to attack the web infrastructure of groups like the Invictus and ADAMSKI. In other words, &quot;war on the internet&quot; is probably a fairly apt way to describe what's going on in the modern World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 07-17-2015, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T10:30:40-07:00","id":593945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=593910#post593910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires are impossible to capture properly on camera (unless they suppress it, iirc) and seeing obvious magic would trigger Quiescence and make you rationalize away what you just saw.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire was just an example. What about the spiders the size of buildings? The ghosts? The rats that burrow into people's chests and ride around in them? The Sin-Eaters and Pandorans and True Fae and Acamoth? The thousands of things that don't have a Masquerade or Masquerade-shielding abilities? Then there's the actual witnesses. A hunter can easily lure a cop or reporter or flash mob to a place where a monster is going to be, let them all be witnesses to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Combine that with the existence of CGI and /shrug. </div> </div> </div>Yes. The Storyteller has to handwave away every proof a Network Zero character comes up with unless they're willing to step into a fallen Masquerade world. Which is why they're a compact of too much potential that has to be constantly curbed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=593942#post593942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Due to the nature of the internet, you don't actually <i>need</i> a global conspiracy to combat a group like Network Zero. Focusing on Vampires for the moment, the writeup for the Mission in <i>Blood and Smoke </i>describes the local Invictus as having seemingly declared war on the internet. They most likely use a combination of automated scripts and human monitors to keep an eye on certain types of web videos, and have agents in the offices of Youtube and Google tasked with making sure that major potential Masquerade breaches get taken down for &quot;terms of service violations.&quot; If the videos wind up being hosted someplace that the Invictus can't shut them down, they can always resort to DDOS attacks or have their agents try to hack the server.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wikileaks archives, the Sony e-mail leaks, the 'Fappening' are all still available for download despite the efforts of governments, corporations and the wealthy. While you can still do it, it's not a matter of information being on one computer anymore, and you unplug it and the information is safe. It's shared across international boundaries. Youtube may be owned by an American company, but there's a variety of other sites that do similar things secretly and in the open.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-17-2015, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T10:59:34-07:00","id":593992,"title":"","content":"I think it's worth keeping in mind that Network Zero is the type of group posting about conspiracies involving inhuman monsters, along with videos of said monsters and pictures and stuff like that, they're more liable to be relegated to the domain of conspiracy theories rather than being taken seriously by the public.<br /> <br /> Not to mention that's not how the Masquerade is contained. The only types of pages the Invictus would ever go after would be ones in which one of the Kindred are somehow doxxed, because the only information you actually need to keep out of the hands of kine is the specific identity of vampires.<br /> <br /> They can post as many blurry videos as they want, it's not gonna magically change the world and make people less skeptical or interested in survival.<br /> <br /> It's not a matter of Network Zero mysteriously having all their videos taken down or anything like that. They post them and mainstream humanity doesn't care. But maybe that video is enough to make them a big deal in the Compact (i.e. higher status as you get notoriety) or <i>other </i>people notice these videos you're putting up, and deduce that you've found the actual supernatural, and they take an interest in you. Maybe that ends poorly.<br /> <br /> I feel obliged to point out that they tend to release information to the public via the internet, and the other group that tried using the internet to coordinate, the Union, got massively screwed over my monsters finding their way on and misleading people.<br /> <br /> Network Zero seems like the kind of group that would run into those issues a lot, unless they keep a private corpus of footage and information somewhere too, maybe some kind of backup site only members can access. Then they occupy a weird space as a group discounted by the &quot;public&quot; insofar as they know about them for batshit conspiracy theories, but they're a potent resource for hunters.<br /> <br /> I'm not really seeing where there's loss of potential in all of that. You <i>don't </i>have to block what the characters do. It's like that sidebar in Precinct 13, you don't have to keep the cops from finding out &quot;a vampire killed this person&quot; because anybody who values their job is not gonna put that in their report. Their higher ups don't want it happening either, not because they're plants by the vampires, but because having a police officer saying that on record makes the whole department look bad.<br /> <br /> The Masquerade is porous and self-repairing, if you think the problem is that they're just one weird internet video away from the World of Darkness Revealed, then you're being way too optimistic about how people receive internet videos that posit conspiracies and other wacky ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T12:12:01-07:00","id":594038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=593945#post593945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampire was just an example. What about the spiders the size of buildings? The ghosts? The rats that burrow into people's chests and ride around in them? The Sin-Eaters and Pandorans and True Fae and Acamoth? The thousands of things that don't have a Masquerade or Masquerade-shielding abilities?</div> </div> </div> </div>What about them? I don't believe that there are physical gods or men in super-tech suits just because I saw the <i>Avengers</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then there's the actual witnesses. A hunter can easily lure a cop or reporter or flash mob to a place where a monster is going to be, let them all be witnesses to it. </div> </div> </div>So you either have a few more people that start to believe <i>or</i> you end up with a bunch of people that now have one more psychological trauma that they actively repress (as per the core books). Mortals don't <i>want</i> to believe, they don't <i>want</i> to know. That's a major factor in why the Masquerade stays up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes. The Storyteller has to handwave away every proof a Network Zero character comes up with unless they're willing to step into a fallen Masquerade world. Which is why they're a compact of too much potential that has to be constantly curbed. </div> </div> </div>It's not a handwave if the entire setting, including both the rules and the fiction, have been set up to explain why it's so.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wikileaks archives, the Sony e-mail leaks, the 'Fappening' are all still available for download despite the efforts of governments, corporations and the wealthy. While you can still do it, it's not a matter of information being on one computer anymore, and you unplug it and the information is safe. It's shared across international boundaries. Youtube may be owned by an American company, but there's a variety of other sites that do similar things secretly and in the open. </div> </div> </div>All three of those involve mundane things people are already willing to believe are true and real (even when they possibly shouldn't with things like some of the Wikileaks stuff).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T15:30:14-07:00","id":594197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=594038#post594038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All three of those involve mundane things people are already willing to believe are true and real (even when they possibly shouldn't with things like some of the Wikileaks stuff).</div> </div> </div> </div>On top of that, those are all things that people are interested in. Huge volumes of celebrity porn get dumped online, and naturally it's going to get downloaded by people all over the world, making it impossible to get rid of. On the other hand, when some anonymous guy's Youtube video about aliens or whatever gets flagged for violating intellectual property laws (and subsequently mysteriously deleted from his hard drive), it's much less likely that there are millions of backups out there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T16:45:50-07:00","id":594268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=594197#post594197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On top of that, those are all things that people are interested in. Huge volumes of celebrity porn get dumped online, and naturally it's going to get downloaded by people all over the world, making it impossible to get rid of. On the other hand, when some anonymous guy's Youtube video about aliens or whatever gets flagged for violating intellectual property laws (and subsequently mysteriously deleted from his hard drive), it's much less likely that there are millions of backups out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, belonging to a group of paranoid conspiracy theorists that think monsters exist is one reasonable reason to keep backups.<br /> <br /> It's just... Nobody believed it the first time you posted it. Why would they believe it next time?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T03:32:40-07:00","id":594610,"title":"","content":"Guys. You do realise that there is already a cannonical explanation for why Network Zero haven't broken the Masqurade.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theonyxpath.com/ill-lie-to-you</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When confronted with the Supernal, whether its rare natural manifestations or, more often, obvious magical effects caused by spells, the Abyss in Sleeper witness\u2019 souls lulls them, forcing them to forget. <b>Other supernatural occurrences</b> don\u2019t provoke the Abyss that obviously, but the Lie still has a subtle effect, predisposing the inhabitants of the World of Darkness to silence, putting the thought of the monsters among them out of mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty much nessacary when you look at some of the stuff The Thief of Masques pulls of; and there's more than one of him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T14:43:10-07:00","id":596091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=594610#post594610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys. You do realise that there is already a cannonical explanation for why Network Zero haven't broken the Masqurade.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's pretty much nessacary when you look at some of the stuff The Thief of Masques pulls of; and there's more than one of him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh look. Somebody who uses Awakening logic to explain a topic that doesn't involve Awakening and give &quot;The Right Answer\u2122&quot;. Bring out the champagne, because heres something I've never seen before...<br /> <br /> I apologise for the snide remark, but the use of Awakening logic to explain everything in all game-lines, outstayed its welcome about a year ago, for me.<br /> Its not a terrible explanation, but wouldn't it make more sense to use Hunters internal logic to explain it, instead of drawing upon a foreign gameline? Maybe Network Zero is actually a puppet organization for a Supernatural agency who uses them to collect intel on other supernaturals, while simultaneously working to make sure that they dont reveal anything to the public?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T17:29:26-07:00","id":596333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=596091#post596091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh look. Somebody who uses Awakening logic to explain a topic that doesn't involve Awakening and give &quot;The Right Answer\u2122&quot;. Bring out the champagne, because heres something I've never seen before...<br /> <br /> I apologise for the snide remark, but the use of Awakening logic to explain everything in all game-lines, outstayed its welcome about a year ago, for me.<br /> Its not a terrible explanation, but wouldn't it make more sense to use Hunters internal logic to explain it, instead of drawing upon a foreign gameline? Maybe Network Zero is actually a puppet organization for a Supernatural agency who uses them to collect intel on other supernaturals, while simultaneously working to make sure that they dont reveal anything to the public?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, hey look, here's the guy that ignores <i>everything the fuck else posted </i>to bitch about someone referencing MtAw. You'd have a reason to be frustrated if that was the <i>only</i> explanation given, but it's not, other explanations were given as well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T00:00:11-07:00","id":596572,"title":"","content":"There's a difference between saying that Awakening explains all gamelines and a thing from Awakening exists in all game lines. The Lie showing up in other games doesn't contradict or attempt to explain those setting's own mythologies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T03:06:37-07:00","id":596662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=596572#post596572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a difference between saying that Awakening explains all gamelines and a thing from Awakening exists in all game lines. The Lie showing up in other games doesn't contradict or attempt to explain those setting's own mythologies.</div> </div> </div> </div>But does it show up though? There are things that works very simillarily to The Lie in other game lines, but they're all given explanations useing the internal logic of those game lines, instead of referencing outside material.<br /> Thats really what I objected to. Not the fact that something simmilar to The Lie could be playing a part in keeping Network Zero from exposing the supernatural, but rather why it needed to be explained useing the internal logic of Awakening.<br /> <br /> I agree with much of whats been written above, although I must say I never had much love for Network Zero at all. It would be so infinitely easy for them to break the entire Masquarade. Find an artifact or friendly supernatural? Go to a labratory and find a scientist willing to help you prove, that this thing doesn't obey the laws of nature. Have him publish a paper about it and do speeches.<br /> It seems to be one of those Compacts thats more of a singularily cool character concept, rather than a whole group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T04:35:45-07:00","id":596709,"title":"","content":"you know that one of the reasons that Network-0 doesn't break and &quot;Masqueraded&quot; (which is, actually, a Vampire term not used in the lexicon of any other gameline. Like the Lie. Just wanted to point it out) is that the compact<i> turn upon itself</i>. They have a whole faction which tries to hide information from the general public. They lack a single leadership, which means that the different factions usually don't work together. You don't need some evil mastermind to control the group in order to stop their efforts- they do it fine by themselves.<br /> <br /> Also, you need to remember that we are talking about people on the internet. Do you believe any crappy video you see online? Heck, I even doubt things I read in National Geographic's website! Why? Because I know that things which show up on the internet could easily be misinterpreted. Last time I've checked, there are real vampires in New Orleans, Megalodon is eating whales, slenderman climbs sky scrappers and there are tongue eating crabs in our tuna. Any sane people would look at it and say &quot;come on!&quot;. Now, if that was the World of Darkness, chances are that those things are at least half true- yet people would still won't believe not because some hot shot vampire is pulling the strings (which is true, and that makes things even more complicated to proof), but because people are not willing to believe in them. Mages call that inborn cynicism &quot;the Lie&quot; and blame the shard of the Abyss in the Sleeper Soul, because that's what mages do- they give big and shiny names to things they don't understand. Most people would just call it &quot;human nature&quot; or a &quot;product of the Western Culture&quot;, because we all love to blame humanity, the Western Culture or both for everything which is bad in the world.<br /> <br /> The point is, that the idea of a group who uploads real monster videos to the internet and fails to convince the world that they are right does not breaks my &quot;suspension of disbelief&quot;. Between lack of organization, infighting, efforts of supernatural beings and groups (including other hunters) to stay hidden and pure human arrogance mixed with cynicism, the chances of such a group to actually proof anything are slim, but they still try. Why? Because they are hunters, and that's what hunters do- they fight against all chances, be it by gun, by prayer, by wand or by a click on the mouse. That's all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T06:08:12-07:00","id":596804,"title":"","content":"But all it takes is for 1 person to do what I described (find a credible professional to look at your data and publish the conclusion) and the entire thing comes tumbling down. Far as I remember, Network Zero isn't solely based on internet videos on Youtube, thats just one avenue.<br /> I mean, its a legit issue in general. All it really takes for the masquarade to fall, is for 1 person to act out of line in an intelligent and coordinated enough manner, and the thing is bunked. Thats not usually an issue, because most of the supernatural types have very good reasons to stay under the radar, but Network Zeros entire thing is that they try to reveal the supernatural element to the world. I find it difficult to believe that a group of (suposedly) intelligent and professional people cant get the message out, without some vast conspiracy tripping them up, or a supernatural entity fucking with them.<br /> It would be like if I had uncovered a new scientific principle that utterly shattered all preconcieved notions of how the field in question operated, and I wanted to get that published and accepted. Sure, I would meet some opposition from the people who enjoy the old paradigm, but without some consserted effort being put into silencing me by a third party, the message would get out one way or the other. Literally all I would need to do, was walk up the university buildings, find a professor thats not currently hella busy with something, and pressent my findings.<br /> <br /> The fact of the matter is, that Network Zero isn't just a group of angry Youtubers who upload videos to the internet. They're suposed to be a group of people who want to reveal the supernatural and one avenue of doing that, is uploading stuff to the internet. Argueably, thats an extreamly inefficient way of revealing anything to anyone, so I find it hard to believe that none of them have used their brains for 2 secounds, and revealised that there are far more efficient methods of accomplishing their goal.<br /> <br /> As I said, I never liked Network Zero. I think they could easily be refitted into a branch of the government, which deals with covert intelligence gathering and obsfucation. Sorta like a CIA for supernatural shenanigans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T09:51:05-07:00","id":597043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=596662#post596662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But does it show up though? There are things that works very simillarily to The Lie in other game lines, but they're all given explanations useing the internal logic of those game lines, instead of referencing outside material.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, they're often not given any explenation at all. They're just there.<br /> <br /> Take this section from The Union in Compacts and Conspiracies<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The truth about the World of Darkness is this: people know. They know it\u2019s a bad place, and that the shadows are long. They suspect that the monsters are real, not metaphor. But they\u2019re scared. Alone. It\u2019s easier to live in ignorance and walk in the bright light of the day and not give power to your fears by acknowledging them. </div> </div> </div>But nothing explains why WoD mortals use force ignorance. It's not normal human reactions, ok it's for some people, but you also get people who hide from their fears by very loudly boasting how not scared they are. Imagine a bunch of people in the pub boasting that they dare any vampire to show his face in here.<br /> <br /> Forced ignorance doesn't need explaining, forced ignorance being universal enough that you'd be ostracised and laughed at for breaking the silence does need an explanation. Hunter doesn't give one.<br /> <br /> To the best of my knowledge the only explanations are Mage's Lie and I think I read something about the God Machine somewhere. <hr /><br /> Also. Network Zero are awesome. Though I think that they should stay.<br /> <br /> However I think &quot;breaking the Masqurade&quot; should be downplayed. Instead I'd make the Record Keepers mostly interested in people who already believe in the supernatural. They want to grow their youtube channels and get status in their online community, make money, get a boy/girlfriend or something like that. Alternatively they're doing it out of genuine belief in some sacred journalistic duty.<br /> <br /> Most Record Keepers should believe that there's already enough evidence out there so breaking the masqurade won't work. The Army of Truth however are fanatics who believe that they can Break the Masqurade if they only got the one perfect video. Or maybe if they hacked their video into the middle of the superbowl.<br /> <br /> As for the Secret Keepers - I've got no idea why they're in Net0 rather than their own group. Crazy survivialists is an unfilled hunter niche (well Skin and Bones has some)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T17:37:31-07:00","id":597554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=596804#post596804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But all it takes is for 1 person to do what I described (find a credible professional to look at your data and publish the conclusion) and the entire thing comes tumbling down. Far as I remember, Network Zero isn't solely based on internet videos on Youtube, thats just one avenue.<br /> I mean, its a legit issue in general. All it really takes for the masquarade to fall, is for 1 person to act out of line in an intelligent and coordinated enough manner, and the thing is bunked. Thats not usually an issue, because most of the supernatural types have very good reasons to stay under the radar, but Network Zeros entire thing is that they try to reveal the supernatural element to the world. I find it difficult to believe that a group of (suposedly) intelligent and professional people cant get the message out, without some vast conspiracy tripping them up, or a supernatural entity fucking with them.<br /> It would be like if I had uncovered a new scientific principle that utterly shattered all preconcieved notions of how the field in question operated, and I wanted to get that published and accepted. Sure, I would meet some opposition from the people who enjoy the old paradigm, but without some consserted effort being put into silencing me by a third party, the message would get out one way or the other. Literally all I would need to do, was walk up the university buildings, find a professor thats not currently hella busy with something, and pressent my findings.<br /> <br /> The fact of the matter is, that Network Zero isn't just a group of angry Youtubers who upload videos to the internet. They're suposed to be a group of people who want to reveal the supernatural and one avenue of doing that, is uploading stuff to the internet. Argueably, thats an extreamly inefficient way of revealing anything to anyone, so I find it hard to believe that none of them have used their brains for 2 secounds, and revealised that there are far more efficient methods of accomplishing their goal.<br /> <br /> As I said, I never liked Network Zero. I think they could easily be refitted into a branch of the government, which deals with covert intelligence gathering and obsfucation. Sorta like a CIA for supernatural shenanigans.</div> </div> </div> </div>You want a scientist to run scientific tests on an item of pure magic (phenomenal or supernal)? Those things that, by their very nature, cause Integrity Breaking Points and a not so slow slide into insanity for those that try to unlock their arcane, and non-scientifically verifiable secrets?<br /> <br /> This isn't even a Science vs Magic thing, it's that the vast majority of scientists that <i>aren't</i> already part of a supernaturally aware group (and thus mostly invested in maintaining the masquerade) will not have sufficient data to explain what they see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 07-22-2015, 02:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T01:47:43-07:00","id":598061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=596804#post596804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But all it takes is for 1 person to do what I described (find a credible professional to look at your data and publish the conclusion) and the entire thing comes tumbling down. Far as I remember, Network Zero isn't solely based on internet videos on Youtube, thats just one avenue.<br /> I mean, its a legit issue in general. All it really takes for the masquarade to fall, is for 1 person to act out of line in an intelligent and coordinated enough manner, and the thing is bunked. Thats not usually an issue, because most of the supernatural types have very good reasons to stay under the radar, but Network Zeros entire thing is that they try to reveal the supernatural element to the world. I find it difficult to believe that a group of (suposedly) intelligent and professional people cant get the message out, without some vast conspiracy tripping them up, or a supernatural entity fucking with them.<br /> It would be like if I had uncovered a new scientific principle that utterly shattered all preconcieved notions of how the field in question operated, and I wanted to get that published and accepted. Sure, I would meet some opposition from the people who enjoy the old paradigm, but without some consserted effort being put into silencing me by a third party, the message would get out one way or the other. Literally all I would need to do, was walk up the university buildings, find a professor thats not currently hella busy with something, and pressent my findings.</div> </div> </div> </div>no, it does not.<br /> <br /> Finding one scientist to work on your side would not make a difference. Why? Because science doesn't work that way.<br /> <br /> First, science is about a research- and a real scientist would need years of research before publishing some sort of article about anything, especially something which is so controversial like &quot;supernatural phenomena&quot;. No real scientist in the world would endanger his or her good name in such a way unless he or she has a very good reason to do so- which means that the scientist would want to keep the item, in his or her possession as long as possible to discover all possible information about the phenomena. The scientist would then ask for more &quot;research subjects&quot;, because he can't write an article just about one item. He would then wait, consult, read, connect the dots, ask for finance in a way that wouldn't make him look crazy (because all that research takes money) until, eventually, if no one would steal the item, threat him or kill him- he would publish an article.<br /> <br /> And become a living joke.<br /> <br /> The scientist is not alone, after all- there are other scientists, many which are financed by supernatural beings. Even honest ones would doubt his theory simply because that's what scientists do. Worse, New Agers would embrace his research, something which is the scientist's worst nightmare. He would feel a lot of pressure to retract his findings and say it was a &quot;mistake&quot; or that things were &quot;out of context&quot;. He would also suffer threats for his life. Maybe he'll put his research on the internet, people would talk about it and laugh, never to mention his name again. Plus, he would never try to present it as a &quot;supernatural&quot; phenomena- but would try to build an whole paradigm to make it into a &quot;natural&quot; one. Why? Because that's what scientists do.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying he won't succeed- it is possible that he may, somehow, manage to convince humanity that the supernatural exist. But it would take a lifetime to do so, and the chances are not in his favor. Just look around you- companies put a lot of money in scientists so they would make researches that support their claims, like that there was always a lot of Lead around you, or that the Global Warming is a natural thing. Now imagine that not only that the someone pays scientists to say that the Global Warming is not a thing, but that every time you try to investigate it, the phenomena itself tries to hide from you! In short, the only way that a single scientist would make a difference is if that scientist is confident, resourceful and willing to endanger everything for his own truth- which mean, that he is a PC. NPCs would never make that difference. And you know whats the problem with being a PC, right?<br /> <br /> That the ST is trying to kill you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T03:35:17-07:00","id":598131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=598061#post598061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> no, it does not.<br /> <br /> Finding one scientist to work on your side would not make a difference. Why? Because science doesn't work that way.<br /> <br /> First, science is about a research- and a real scientist would need years of research before publishing some sort of article about anything, especially something which is so controversial like &quot;supernatural phenomena&quot;. No real scientist in the world would endanger his or her good name in such a way unless he or she has a very good reason to do so- which means that the scientist would want to keep the item, in his or her possession as long as possible to discover all possible information about the phenomena. The scientist would then ask for more &quot;research subjects&quot;, because he can't write an article just about one item. He would then wait, consult, read, connect the dots, ask for finance in a way that wouldn't make him look crazy (because all that research takes money) until, eventually, if no one would steal the item, threat him or kill him- he would publish an article.<br /> <br /> And become a living joke.<br /> <br /> The scientist is not alone, after all- there are other scientists, many which are financed by supernatural beings. Even honest ones would doubt his theory simply because that's what scientists do. Worse, New Agers would embrace his research, something which is the scientist's worst nightmare. He would feel a lot of pressure to retract his findings and say it was a &quot;mistake&quot; or that things were &quot;out of context&quot;. He would also suffer threats for his life. Maybe he'll put his research on the internet, people would talk about it and laugh, never to mention his name again. Plus, he would never try to present it as a &quot;supernatural&quot; phenomena- but would try to build an whole paradigm to make it into a &quot;natural&quot; one. Why? Because that's what scientists do.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying he won't succeed- it is possible that he may, somehow, manage to convince humanity that the supernatural exist. But it would take a lifetime to do so, and the chances are not in his favor. Just look around you- companies put a lot of money in scientists so they would make researches that support their claims, like that there was always a lot of Lead around you, or that the Global Warming is a natural thing. Now imagine that not only that the someone pays scientists to say that the Global Warming is not a thing, but that every time you try to investigate it, the phenomena itself tries to hide from you! In short, the only way that a single scientist would make a difference is if that scientist is confident, resourceful and willing to endanger everything for his own truth- which mean, that he is a PC. NPCs would never make that difference. And you know whats the problem with being a PC, right?<br /> <br /> That the ST is trying to kill you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I agree with your acessment. If I found something 'supernatural' I would show it to my fellow students and the professors who lecture me. All of those people know very well that I am a pretty smart physicist and a number of them know that I have very little patience for anything 'supernatural'. Sure, they might find it laughable at first, but I am pretty sure they would atleast give me the time of day to take a look at it.<br /> My point is, that yes, a single scientist wont do much, but if you can convince 1 scientist then chances are you've also made good headway to convincing his network. They respect him and probably wont reject the findings outright. I am confident that the majority of university scientists would want to &quot;endanger&quot; their name, if they found a paradigm shifting phenomenon, as this would be. We've actually seen it before with scientists having done precisely that.<br /> I totally agree that it would be an uphill struggle, but if he had hard and fast proof of his assertion - an artifact or actual supernatural creature - it would pretty much ensure his success, unless some third party stepped in to stop him.<br /> I kinda agree that such a character borderlines a PC, but I think it could reasonably be modeled by a high-dot rating Retainer or Ally. Then again. I've never been a fan of removing agency from the NPCs just because the PCs are technically 'the main characters'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1958,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","user":"Krobeles","date":". 07-22-2015, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T04:53:24-07:00","id":598160,"title":"","content":"And then comes Invictus, Iron Masters, Guardians of Veil, Winter Court and rest of &quot;supernatural secret services&quot;. Not too mentioned hunters of Loyalists of Thule or Null Mysteriies that wanted to shut you out just so they could still conduct their research in safe and secret, without above monsters conspiracies in the way. Your characters ( PCs and NPCs ) does not live in vacuum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T07:02:24-07:00","id":598275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=598160#post598160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then comes Invictus, Iron Masters, Guardians of Veil, Winter Court and rest of &quot;supernatural secret services&quot;. Not too mentioned hunters of Loyalists of Thule or Null Mysteriies that wanted to shut you out just so they could still conduct their research in safe and secret, without above monsters conspiracies in the way. Your characters ( PCs and NPCs ) does not live in vacuum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well thats precisely what I was saying. It only makes sense if you assume that a third party conspiracy is constantly tripping them up, making sure to foil all their work, which in turn becomes a major annoyance for the players who will constantly have all their work and effort dashed, in order to not break one of the underlying pillars of the World of Darkness.<br /> Sure, that could be an interesting story in its own right, having the players flee and hide from the vast supernatural conspiracies who want to hunt them down and murder them to protect their secrecy, but then thats not really playing into the whole &quot;revealing the supernatural&quot; thing, which Network Zero ostensibly aim to nail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T23:22:52-07:00","id":599056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=598131#post598131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure I agree with your acessment. If I found something 'supernatural' I would show it to my fellow students and the professors who lecture me. All of those people know very well that I am a pretty smart physicist and a number of them know that I have very patience for anything 'supernatural'. Sure, they might find it laughable at first, but I am pretty sure they would atleast give me the time of day to take a look at it.<br /> My point is, that yes, a single scientist wont do much, but if you can convince 1 scientist then chances are you've also made good headway to convincing his network. They respect him and probably wont reject the findings outright. I am confident that the majority of university scientists would want to &quot;endanger&quot; their name, if they found a paradigm shifting phenomenon, as this would be. We've actually seen it before with scientists having done precisely that.<br /> I totally agree that it would be an uphill struggle, but if he had hard and fast proof of his assertion - an artifact or actual supernatural creature - it would pretty much ensure his success, unless some third party stepped in to stop him.<br /> I kinda agree that such a character borderlines a PC, but I think it could reasonably be modeled by a high-dot rating Retainer or Ally. Then again. I've never been a fan of removing agency from the NPCs just because the PCs are technically 'the main characters'.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are <i>still</i> assuming that:<br /> 1) The item in question is testable in a way that meets scientific rigor<br /> 2) the scientist(s) won't <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/GoMadFromTheRevelation\" target=\"_blank\">go mad from the revelation</a>, and<br /> 3) the item in question, its previous possessor, or its future would-be possessor (or a combination thereof) aren't actively inimical towards the aforementioned scientist(s).<br /> <br /> As we are dealing with magic of an unspecified variety, none of those assumptions are warranted or even likely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T00:27:21-07:00","id":599069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=599056#post599056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) The item in question is testable in a way that meets scientific rigor</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, just to give an example, Vitae and blood look different under a microscope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T02:30:46-07:00","id":599102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=599056#post599056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are <i>still</i> assuming that:<br /> 1) The item in question is testable in a way that meets scientific rigor<br /> 2) the scientist(s) won't <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/GoMadFromTheRevelation\" target=\"_blank\">go mad from the revelation</a>, and<br /> 3) the item in question, its previous possessor, or its future would-be possessor (or a combination thereof) aren't actively inimical towards the aforementioned scientist(s).<br /> <br /> As we are dealing with magic of an unspecified variety, none of those assumptions are warranted or even likely.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) If it exists, its testable, if only to conclude that it disobeys a scientific law or two, which is largely the point. Sure, if nobody can activate it, thats an issue, but then he should find a better item.<br /> 2) This the World of Darkness. Not a Lovecraft novel. People dont go mad from supernatural revelations, as far as the World of Darkness is concerned. Maybe loose a point of Integrity if its real bad, but thats hardly going mad.<br /> 3) And again we're back to my point of &quot;unless a third party staunchs him&quot;<br /> <br /> This is actually a larger issue, I find. What if your players all suddenly decide they want to go public? Whats stopping your group of Mages/Vampires/Werewolfs/Sin-Eaters/Changelings/Whatevers from going to Times Square and doing all sorts of supernatural shenanigans? Sure, the Werewolfs has the Lunacy and Mages have The Lie to make people more likely to forget, but even those aren't 100% fool proof and the rest of them dont even have anything of the sort. Whats to stop your player group from breaking this pillar quite immidiately?<br /> This goes for a Hunter group too, if they have Endowments. Whats to stop a Malefictum Hunter from attending an Atheist convention and calling upon the power of god to once and for all prove his existence to the people there? Whats to stop an Acending One from going to a pharmaceutical company with his quasi-supernatural drugs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T07:23:47-07:00","id":599358,"title":"","content":"Truth be told, there is nothing really stopping a group of PC's with enough gumption with walking into a live taping of the local news and killing everyone is an obviously supernatural manner. The ST would just have to navigate A) Why would they do such a thing? Living in the shadows is too the benefit of most supernaturals and quasi-superanturals. And B) Whats the Fallout? If you are interested in running the aftermath of that revelation, go for it (it sounds like alot of fun).<br /> <br /> As far as the bigger concern of why the lid hasn't been blown off the whole thing already, I always apply the rule that masquerade is self-enforcing. Especially in the new world of darkness, the monsters don't run the world, so it would be impossible to plug every leak. However, their biggest co-conspirator is humanity itself. People typically won't believe, even when confronted with glaring proof. On some gut level, your typical person in the world of darkness [where the monsters are real and always have been] feels that if they can see the monsters, <i>then the monsters can see them right back</i>. And most right thinking people would prefer to live their lives without that kind of attention.<br /> <br /> Any character or organization whose goal it is to expose the World of Darkness has not only that hurdle, but just about every other hurdle mentioned in this thread [ cynicism, skepticism, organized opposition, and the tendency for the phenomena itself to defy explanation and resist documentation].<br /> <br /> We live in a world where people think evolution is BS, Global Warming is a lie made up by the left, and immunizations cause autism. Even damning proof about the existence of the supernatural might take decades before it is accepted, and the whole time the monsters themselves would be doing damage control on an unprecedented level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T08:51:19-07:00","id":599481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=599102#post599102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) If it exists, its testable, if only to conclude that it disobeys a scientific law or two, which is largely the point. Sure, if nobody can activate it, thats an issue, but then he should find a better item.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming it obeys laws of causality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) This the World of Darkness. Not a Lovecraft novel. People dont go mad from supernatural revelations, as far as the World of Darkness is concerned. Maybe loose a point of Integrity if its real bad, but thats hardly going mad. </div> </div> </div>Actually, people <i>do</i> go mad from supernatural revelations, it's <i>always</i> a breaking point for a Mortal without a minor supernatural merit and often a breaking point even with. Extended contact would cause lots of breaking points.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) And again we're back to my point of &quot;unless a third party staunchs him&quot; </div> </div> </div>Stymies? And if you're completely against 3rd parties, then the whole thing is moot because it requires lots of third parties to help them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is actually a larger issue, I find. What if your players all suddenly decide they want to go public? Whats stopping your group of Mages/Vampires/Werewolfs/Sin-Eaters/Changelings/Whatevers from going to Times Square and doing all sorts of supernatural shenanigans? Sure, the Werewolfs has the Lunacy and Mages have The Lie to make people more likely to forget, but even those aren't 100% fool proof and the rest of them dont even have anything of the sort. Whats to stop your player group from breaking this pillar quite immidiately?<br /> This goes for a Hunter group too, if they have Endowments. Whats to stop a Malefictum Hunter from attending an Atheist convention and calling upon the power of god to once and for all prove his existence to the people there? Whats to stop an Acending One from going to a pharmaceutical company with his quasi-supernatural drugs? </div> </div> </div>People perform street magic and shit all the time, obviously it was all some sort of magic trick. I mean, I once saw a magician make an entire plane disappear!<br /> <br /> The Malleus Maleficarum are part of the Catholic Church and have Rules against that sort of thing. The Ascending One's drugs don't work on anyone but Ascending Ones, they're just poison to anyone else.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T09:39:29-07:00","id":599532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=599481#post599481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Assuming it obeys laws of causality.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Actually, people <i>do</i> go mad from supernatural revelations, it's <i>always</i> a breaking point for a Mortal without a minor supernatural merit and often a breaking point even with. Extended contact would cause lots of breaking points.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Stymies? And if you're completely against 3rd parties, then the whole thing is moot because it requires lots of third parties to help them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> People perform street magic and shit all the time, obviously it was all some sort of magic trick. I mean, I once saw a magician make an entire plane disappear!<br /> <br /> The Malleus Maleficarum are part of the Catholic Church and have Rules against that sort of thing. The Ascending One's drugs don't work on anyone but Ascending Ones, they're just poison to anyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much every magical item as written in the source material, obeys causality without error or exception. If you found an item that breaks that general trend, its probably some horrible abyssal blasphemy from outside time and space, and its detrimental, catatrosphic effects on linear time is much more important than what we're currently discussing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Just because its a Breaking Point, hardly means he'll go mad. As written in the 2ed rules, a person with high Resolve+Composure hardly needs to worry about Breaking Points, unless he witnesses something truely horrific, which a sterile test in an enviroment he is familliar with, certainly is not.<br /> <br /> Yeah, but street magic is street magic. I've hardly seen a person turn 20 meters tall, grow a third arm and fly away by reciting verses in a language I dont understand. I think it'de be pretty difficult to explain that away.<br /> The Catholic Church also has rules about rapeing underaged boys, but alas here we are.<br /> The thing about The Ascending Ones drugs, is that they nessesarily have some kind of physical component to them, which can be studied. Obviously, certain mixtures of chemicals, combined with the proper mental state (probably some brain chemistry there) can trigger certain physical effects, which should be very possible to be studied. Yes, its poison to most normal people, but thats also one of the things which makes it very easy to study, if you found an Ascending One willing to help you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T10:13:52-07:00","id":599597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=599481#post599481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming it obeys laws of causality.</div> </div> </div> </div> Most supernatural powers do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=599481#post599481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, people <i>do</i> go mad from supernatural revelations, it's <i>always</i> a breaking point for a Mortal without a minor supernatural merit and often a breaking point even with. Extended contact would cause lots of breaking points.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hunters will have some kind of protection.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=599481#post599481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Malleus Maleficarum are part of the Catholic Church and have Rules against that sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div> Those rules are probably &quot;think first&quot; not &quot;never ever&quot;. Jesus Himself performed miracles to advertise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=599481#post599481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Ascending One's drugs don't work on anyone but Ascending Ones, they're just poison to anyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually they do. Look at Mesmeric Vapors, works on anyone.<br /> <br /> The poison is a from of anti-theft protection plus a philosophical statement. Not an integral part of how the magic functions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T13:35:39-07:00","id":599741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=599532#post599532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty much every magical item as written in the source material, obeys causality without error or exception. If you found an item that breaks that general trend, its probably some horrible abyssal blasphemy from outside time and space, and its detrimental, catatrosphic effects on linear time is much more important than what we're currently discussing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much every magical item as written in the source material is almost impossible to use reliably by a baseline Mortal and is thus untestable (since they can't turn it on). They require special merits or templates to use, and if you have that template/merit you're most likely &quot;in&quot; on the masquerade.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just because its a Breaking Point, hardly means he'll go mad. As written in the 2ed rules, a person with high Resolve+Composure hardly needs to worry about Breaking Points, unless he witnesses something truely horrific, which a sterile test in an enviroment he is familliar with, certainly is not. </div> </div> </div>Assuming he can use it (a pretty major assumption), every time he attempts to test it will cause a breaking point. Eventually he'll fail multiple times <i>or</i> will start to develop some sort of supernatural weirdness. In the latter case they're no longer baseline mortals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, but street magic is street magic. I've hardly seen a person turn 20 meters tall, grow a third arm and fly away </div> </div> </div>Spiked drink.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> by reciting verses in a language I dont understand. </div> </div> </div>Because you know every language ever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it'de be pretty difficult to explain that away. </div> </div> </div>Someone spiked your drink and another person spoke gibberish/a language you don't know (of which there are a lot). Or there was a gas leak. Fuck, dude, there are people that believe the Moon Landings were faked and there's real evidence for that, you're talking about stuff most people know is nonsense as if it must be irrefutable on the thinnest of evidence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Catholic Church also has rules about rapeing underaged boys, but alas here we are. </div> </div> </div>The real Catholic Church also doesn't have magic to enforce its rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The thing about The Ascending Ones drugs, is that they nessesarily have some kind of physical component to them, which can be studied. Obviously, certain mixtures of chemicals, combined with the proper mental state (probably some brain chemistry there) can trigger certain physical effects, which should be very possible to be studied. Yes, its poison to most normal people, but thats also one of the things which makes it very easy to study, if you found an Ascending One willing to help you. </div> </div> </div>That's a lot of ifs, and you assume that the alchemical compound would appear as anything other than an inert mixture with poison under scientific tests. Even if you did have an Ascending One helping you (<i>now</i> who's assuming the existence of outside groups?), that doesn't mean that the alchemical solution is magical, just that there's something weird going on that can't be isolated.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=599597#post599597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Most supernatural powers do.</div> </div> </div> </div>As in my response to Krobeles: even those that do follow causality don't generally work for Mortals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hunters will have some kind of protection. </div> </div> </div>External group.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Those rules are probably &quot;think first&quot; not &quot;never ever&quot;. Jesus Himself performed miracles to advertise. </div> </div> </div>Or Jesus was a charlatan and huckster. Or his &quot;disciples&quot; wrote fanfiction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually they do. Look at Mesmeric Vapors, works on anyone. </div> </div> </div>Mesmeric Vapors only gains magical properties after being inhaled by the Ascending One, otherwise it causes the same effects as opium or a toxin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The poison is a from of anti-theft protection plus a philosophical statement. Not an integral part of how the magic functions. </div> </div> </div>But the Ascending Ones don't know how to make it <i>without </i>the toxic aspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 07-22-2015, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T14:45:15-07:00","id":599839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=599741#post599741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much every magical item as written in the source material is almost impossible to use reliably by a baseline Mortal and is thus untestable (since they can't turn it on). They require special merits or templates to use, and if you have that template/merit you're most likely &quot;in&quot; on the masquerade.</div> </div> </div> </div> Objectively wrong. Or please point to the section in the AKD's Relic Endowment or the Reliquary book that says this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=599741#post599741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As in my response to Krobeles: even those that do follow causality don't generally work for Mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div> Wrong. Hunter Endowments. Second Sight Thamaturgy. Psychic phenomina (if you have a handy psychic). Relics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=599741#post599741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">External group.</div> </div> </div> </div> No, The Code.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=599741#post599741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or Jesus was a charlatan and huckster. Or his &quot;disciples&quot; wrote fanfiction.</div> </div> </div> </div> Tell that to the Catholic Church.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=599741#post599741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mesmeric Vapors only gains magical properties after being inhaled by the Ascending One, otherwise it causes the same effects as opium or a toxin.</div> </div> </div> </div> I know. The Ascending One takes the poison out, and then it works on anyone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=599741#post599741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Ascending Ones don't know how to make it <i>without </i>the toxic aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course they do. Where do you think the recipies came from in the first place?<br /> <br /> The Ascending Ones develop them, and if they can develop working alchemy they can develop it without poison. Note that in their origin story they did so, and then decided it was better with poison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T15:30:47-07:00","id":599870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=599597#post599597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The poison is a from of anti-theft protection plus a philosophical statement. Not an integral part of how the magic functions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this explicitly stated somewhere? I've been operating under the assumption that Ascending Ones' potions just have harmful side effects (like most drugs), which members of the conspiracy have painstakingly developed a resistance to.<br /> <br /> In any event, with regard to how the supernatural is kept under wraps in the nWoD, there are two things that seem to cove through in most of the literature:<br /> <br /> 1. It kind of isn't. The evidence is there if people want to look for it, but most don't because, firstly, people are mostly concerned with their own day to day lives and don't really want to know about the sinister stuff going on in their back yard, and secondly, those who have some inkling of what's going on learn quickly that things tend to go very badly for people who dig too deep.<br /> <br /> 2. There are lots and lots of forces at work trying to maintain the masquerade, or at least shut down major breaches. Here are some of the more active ones:<br /> <br /> - The Invictus (who have mind and memory altering powers and lots and lots of money)<br /> - At least two of the major orders of Mages (who have mind, memory, and <i>reality</i> altering powers)<br /> - Werewolves in general (who mess up peoples' memories just by being around them, and have absolutely no compunction about killing people who know too much)<br /> - The Exarchs<br /> - Probably some Archmages<br /> - The sliver of the Abyss that lurks inside almost every human soul<br /> - Shadowy government conspiracies<br /> - The Wyrd<br /> - Fate (evidently not exactly the same thing as the Wyrd)<br /> - The God Machine<br /> - The Storyteller (in most cases)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 07-22-2015, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T15:40:17-07:00","id":599873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=599870#post599870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this explicitly stated somewhere? I've been operating under the assumption that Ascending Ones' potions just have harmful side effects (like most drugs), which members of the conspiracy have painstakingly developed a resistance to.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's stated that the alchemy <i>could</i> work sans-poison, but that the Ascending Ones 1) don't know this and 2) wouldn't know how to make it non-toxic even if they did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T22:03:18-07:00","id":600178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=599839#post599839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Objectively wrong. Or please point to the section in the AKD's Relic Endowment or the Reliquary book that says this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Objectively true: MOST don't work for Mortals without special conditions. A small number, such as the very small number of AKD's relics, work without any special ability.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wrong. Hunter Endowments. Second Sight Thamaturgy. Psychic phenomina (if you have a handy psychic). Relics. </div> </div> </div>True: most Hunter Endowments aren't artifacts, Second Sight Thaumaturgy isn't an artifact, Psychic phenomena aren't artifacts. Only Relics are artifacts, they make up a small portion of the printed supernatural items in nWoD, and the AKD <i>does not</i> want to pull back the masquerade so they <i>will</i> be actively working to maintain it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, The Code. </div> </div> </div>The Hunter Code (such as it is) will not protect Joe Random non-Hunter scientist that your Net0 member has foisted this item off on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tell that to the Catholic Church. </div> </div> </div>'K.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know. The Ascending One takes the poison out, and then it works on anyone. </div> </div> </div>They don't know how.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course they do. Where do you think the recipies came from in the first place? </div> </div> </div>Rote memorization.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Ascending Ones develop them, and if they can develop working alchemy they can develop it without poison. Note that in their origin story they did so, and then decided it was better with poison. </div> </div> </div>The original ones decided this, all the other learn the formulas by rote.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T00:25:43-07:00","id":600267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=599870#post599870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this explicitly stated somewhere? I've been operating under the assumption that Ascending Ones' potions just have harmful side effects (like most drugs), which members of the conspiracy have painstakingly developed a resistance to.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes. Their opening history talks about their founders. One creates a poition with no poison then kills himself from over use.<br /> <br /> So the next founder added poison so he wouldn't be tempted to overdo it.<br /> <br /> Now this could be an elabourate post-fact justification because drugs are harmful. However there are alchemists in the WoD who can creation non-toxic potions, and the Ascending Ones keep tabs on alchemists outside their order. so even if the Ascending Ones didn't have recipes for non-toxic elixirs now they could easily get hold of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=599870#post599870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. It kind of isn't. The evidence is there if people want to look for it, but most don't because, firstly, people are mostly concerned with their own day to day lives and don't really want to know about the sinister stuff going on in their back yard, and secondly, those who have some inkling of what's going on learn quickly that things tend to go very badly for people who dig too deep.</div> </div> </div> </div> Exactly.<br /> <br /> And also because WoD people are not like real life people and have an instinctive desire to avoid and not talk about the supernatural. The Abyss is the only time there's an actual reason given for that which I know off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=599870#post599870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- The Wyrd</div> </div> </div> </div>I always imagined the Wyrd likes the Masqurade but also creates Hunters who see past it. In Dream Catcher's it's not explicit but the perfectly timed decomposition of a Fetch that created Searchlight was the Wyrd nudging things along.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=600178#post600178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Objectively true: MOST don't work for Mortals without special conditions. A small number, such as the very small number of AKD's relics, work without any special ability.</div> </div> </div> </div> Citation needed.<br /> <br /> (AKD have enough Relics to give every active hunter multiple ones and still have entire werehouses left over waiting for a player to spend EXP on new tricks)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=600178#post600178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True: most Hunter Endowments aren't artifacts, Second Sight Thaumaturgy isn't an artifact, Psychic phenomena aren't artifacts. Only Relics are artifacts, they make up a small portion of the printed supernatural items in nWoD, and the AKD <i>does not</i> want to pull back the masquerade so they <i>will</i> be actively working to maintain it.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of which stop a scientist studying them. Except the AKD, but they don't have all the Relics.They just think they should.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=600178#post600178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hunter Code (such as it is) will not protect Joe Random non-Hunter scientist that your Net0 member has foisted this item off on.</div> </div> </div> </div> Joe Random scientist has a chance of becoming a hunter. Or take it too Null Mysteriis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=600178#post600178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't know how.</div> </div> </div> </div> Check the RnD rules. They could if they wanted too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=600178#post600178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rote memorization.</div> </div> </div> </div> I said 'first place'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/590340-wasted-potential?p=600178#post600178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The original ones decided this, all the other learn the formulas by rote.</div> </div> </div> </div>You realise that there's explicit rules in Hunter for researching new Elixirs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-23-2015, 03:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T04:28:30-07:00","id":600339,"title":"","content":"Also, it merits pointing out that almost every supernatural artifact that occur outside of a main gameline, can be activated with the expenditure of a point of Willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}